cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ADI (data, rubric, tools or figures), please cite the paper below."
type: dataset
title: "The Delegation Divide: An Open Index of AI-Agent Delegability across Occupations and Countries"
abstract: >-
  Agent Delegability Index (ADI) v2026.1: 18,796 O*NET 30.2 task statements rated on a frozen,
  preregistered four-level rubric (L0 no role, L1 augmentation, L2 partial delegation, L3 full
  delegation) by Claude Sonnet 5.5 and Claude Haiku 5.5, aggregated to 433 ISCO-08 unit groups and
  weighted by ILOSTAT employment for 146 countries. 35.2% of task time in world employment is at
  least partly delegable to AI agents in 2026; 2.5% can be handed over in full.
